@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito-il08-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-il08-tax-years`
IMPORT `ito-il08-published-figures`
IMPORT `ito-s47a-definitions`
IMPORT `ito-s45a-insurance-and-pension-credit`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Tests for s 47(a) (the definitions) and s 45A (the credit). Row IL-08.
--
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the section's text (quoted in the rule modules) and
-- the figures below, before the rules were run; NOTES.md section 5 has the arithmetic. None has been
-- edited to match what the code computed. A failing assertion is a finding.
--
-- THE FIGURES for 2026, as this row's test author takes them: the withholding booklet's monthly
-- figures times twelve (assumption A3, ito-il08-published-figures.l4): s 45A(d)(1) 12 x 189 = 2,268;
-- qualifying-income paragraph (1) 12 x 9,700 = 116,400; paragraph (2) 12 x 13,700 = 164,400; the
-- average wage 12 x 13,769 = 165,228 for the year, so a beneficiary member needs 16% of it, 26,436.48.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Tests — sections 47(a) and 45A`

§§ `The figures`

`the 2026 amounts` MEANS `The amounts of sections 45A and 47 in force in the tax year` WITH
    `the amount in section 45A(d)(1)`                                    IS 2268
    `the amount in paragraph (1) of the definition of qualifying income` IS 116400
    `the amount in paragraph (2) of the definition of qualifying income` IS 164400
    `the average wage in the economy, in total for the tax year`         IS 165228

-- The published-figures module gives the same, field by field.
#ASSERT (`the amounts of sections 45A and 47, as twelve times the Tax Authority's monthly figures, for tax year` 2026)'s `the amount in section 45A(d)(1)` EQUALS 2268
#ASSERT (`the amounts of sections 45A and 47, as twelve times the Tax Authority's monthly figures, for tax year` 2026)'s `the amount in paragraph (1) of the definition of qualifying income` EQUALS 116400
#ASSERT (`the amounts of sections 45A and 47, as twelve times the Tax Authority's monthly figures, for tax year` 2026)'s `the amount in paragraph (2) of the definition of qualifying income` EQUALS 164400
#ASSERT (`the amounts of sections 45A and 47, as twelve times the Tax Authority's monthly figures, for tax year` 2026)'s `the average wage in the economy, in total for the tax year` EQUALS 165228
#ASSERT REFUSED `the amounts of sections 45A and 47, as twelve times the Tax Authority's monthly figures, for tax year` 2023 BECAUSE "no Tax Authority figure for sections 45A and 47 has been sourced for this tax year"

`the 2025 amounts` MEANS `the amounts of sections 45A and 47, as twelve times the Tax Authority's monthly figures, for tax year` 2025
#ASSERT `the 2025 amounts`'s `the average wage in the economy, in total for the tax year` EQUALS 150432

§§ `The people in the tests`

-- Sums for s 45A, positionally, under this ruler:
--                                                      life,  pension, State, survivors, child life, child pension, of which not from work
GIVEN `pension` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Sums paid in the tax year, for section 45A`
`pension sums only:` `pension` MEANS
    `Sums paid in the tax year, for section 45A` OF 0, `pension`, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0

GIVEN `life`    IS A NUMBER
      `pension` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Sums paid in the tax year, for section 45A`
`life insurance and pension:` `life` `,` `pension` MEANS
    `Sums paid in the tax year, for section 45A` OF `life`, `pension`, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0

GIVEN `pension`   IS A NUMBER
      `survivors` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Sums paid in the tax year, for section 45A`
`pension and survivors' insurance:` `pension` `,` `survivors` MEANS
    `Sums paid in the tax year, for section 45A` OF 0, `pension`, 0, `survivors`, 0, 0, 0

GIVEN `pension`       IS A NUMBER
      `not from work` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Sums paid in the tax year, for section 45A`
`pension, with a part paid in respect of income not from work:` `pension` `,` `not from work` MEANS
    `Sums paid in the tax year, for section 45A` OF 0, `pension`, 0, 0, 0, 0, `not from work`

GIVEN `pension`         IS A NUMBER
      `child's pension` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Sums paid in the tax year, for section 45A`
`pension and a child's provident fund:` `pension` `,` `child's pension` MEANS
    `Sums paid in the tax year, for section 45A` OF 0, `pension`, 0, 0, 0, `child's pension`, 0

`no sums for section 47` MEANS `Sums paid in the tax year, for section 47` OF 0, 0, 0, 0

-- An individual. Everything the s 45A(f) and s 47 tests do not need is nil or FALSE.
GIVEN `the year`  IS A NUMBER
      `resident`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `work`      IS A NUMBER
      `other`     IS A NUMBER
      `insured`   IS A NUMBER
      `deposits`  IS A NUMBER
      `the sums`  IS A `Sums paid in the tax year, for section 45A`
      `deducted`  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47`
`in` `the year` `, resident` `resident` `, work income` `work` `, other income` `other` `, insured income` `insured` `, deposits for him` `deposits` `, sums` `the sums` `, deducted under s 47` `deducted` MEANS
    `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47` WITH
        `tax year`                                                                      IS `the year`
        `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                                           IS `resident`
        `taxable income from work, before the deductions under sections 47 and 47A`     IS `work`
        `taxable income not from work, before the deductions under sections 47 and 47A` IS `other`
        `taxable income from a business or profession`                                  IS 0
        `insured income`                                                                IS `insured`
        `sums paid in the tax year to a pension provident fund in respect of the individual's income` IS `deposits`
        `sums paid, for section 45A`                                                    IS `the sums`
        `sums paid, for section 47`                                                     IS `no sums for section 47`
        `sums deducted under section 47(b) or (b1)`                                     IS `deducted`
        `sums deposited to a pension provident fund as a self-employed member for himself, not credited under section 45A(b)` IS 0
        `a deduction was made for him under section 32(14)(b) for preferred insurance against loss of working capacity`      IS FALSE
        `within a class for which regulations under section 47(d) set higher deductions`                                    IS FALSE
        `a foreign worker`                                                                                                  IS FALSE

-- An employee paid the same salary every month, his employer paying for him 6.5% (benefits) and
