`E15, an employee on 15,000 a month, paying 6%` MEANS
    `in` 2026 `, resident` TRUE `, work income` 180000 `, other income` 0 `, insured income` 180000 `, deposits for him` 33300 `, sums` (`pension sums only:` 10800) `, deducted under s 47` 0
`E15, paying 7%` MEANS
    `in` 2026 `, resident` TRUE `, work income` 180000 `, other income` 0 `, insured income` 180000 `, deposits for him` 35100 `, sums` (`pension sums only:` 12600) `, deducted under s 47` 0
`E5, an employee on 5,000 a month, paying 6%` MEANS
    `in` 2026 `, resident` TRUE `, work income` 60000 `, other income` 0 `, insured income` 60000 `, deposits for him` 11100 `, sums` (`pension sums only:` 3600) `, deducted under s 47` 0
`L, a low earner on 20,000 a year, paying 1,200` MEANS
    `in` 2026 `, resident` TRUE `, work income` 20000 `, other income` 0 `, insured income` 20000 `, deposits for him` 3700 `, sums` (`pension sums only:` 1200) `, deducted under s 47` 0

§§ `Section 47(a)(1) — qualifying income`

-- Hand-worked from lines 1766-1768: work income up to 116,400; income not from work up to 164,400
-- less the lower of the work income and 116,400.

GIVEN `work`  IS A NUMBER
      `other` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47`
`a 2026 earner of` `work` `from work and` `other` `otherwise` MEANS
    `in` 2026 `, resident` TRUE `, work income` `work` `, other income` `other` `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 0 `, sums` (`pension sums only:` 0) `, deducted under s 47` 0

-- limb (1): only work income.
#ASSERT `s 47(a)(1) — the qualifying income of` (`a 2026 earner of` 120000 `from work and` 0 `otherwise`) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 116400
#ASSERT `s 47(a)(1) — the qualifying income of` (`a 2026 earner of` 50000 `from work and` 0 `otherwise`) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 50000
-- limb (2): no work income.
#ASSERT `s 47(a)(1) — the qualifying income of` (`a 2026 earner of` 0 `from work and` 200000 `otherwise`) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 164400
#ASSERT `s 47(a)(1) — the qualifying income of` (`a 2026 earner of` 0 `from work and` 90000 `otherwise`) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 90000
-- limb (3): both. 60,000 + min(150,000, 164,400 - 60,000) = 164,400.
#ASSERT `s 47(a)(1) — the qualifying income of` (`a 2026 earner of` 60000 `from work and` 150000 `otherwise`) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 164400
-- 116,400 + min(50,000, 164,400 - 116,400) = 164,400; the work income above 116,400 is not counted
-- and does not use up the room (the lower of the two things deducted is 116,400).
#ASSERT `s 47(a)(1) — the qualifying income of` (`a 2026 earner of` 130000 `from work and` 50000 `otherwise`) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 164400
#ASSERT `s 47(a)(1) — the part of the qualifying income that is not work income:` (`a 2026 earner of` 130000 `from work and` 50000 `otherwise`) `,` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 48000
-- 30,000 + min(10,000, 134,400) = 40,000.
#ASSERT `s 47(a)(1) — the qualifying income of` (`a 2026 earner of` 30000 `from work and` 10000 `otherwise`) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 40000
-- Limb (3)'s general formula gives limb (1)'s and limb (2)'s answers where they overlap.
#ASSERT `s 47(a)(1) — the part of the qualifying income that is work income:` (`a 2026 earner of` 120000 `from work and` 0 `otherwise`) `,` `the 2026 amounts` PLUS `s 47(a)(1) — the part of the qualifying income that is not work income:` (`a 2026 earner of` 120000 `from work and` 0 `otherwise`) `,` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 116400
#ASSERT `s 47(a)(1) — the part of the qualifying income that is work income:` (`a 2026 earner of` 0 `from work and` 200000 `otherwise`) `,` `the 2026 amounts` PLUS `s 47(a)(1) — the part of the qualifying income that is not work income:` (`a 2026 earner of` 0 `from work and` 200000 `otherwise`) `,` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 164400

§§ `Section 47(a)(3) and (5) — income for a self-employed member, additional income`

`S100, self-employed, 100,000` MEANS
    `in` 2026 `, resident` TRUE `, work income` 0 `, other income` 100000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 0 `, sums` (`pension sums only:` 0) `, deducted under s 47` 0
`S250, self-employed, 250,000` MEANS
    `in` 2026 `, resident` TRUE `, work income` 0 `, other income` 250000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 0 `, sums` (`pension sums only:` 0) `, deducted under s 47` 0
`M, 60,000 insured salary and 100,000 otherwise` MEANS
    `in` 2026 `, resident` TRUE `, work income` 60000 `, other income` 100000 `, insured income` 60000 `, deposits for him` 0 `, sums` (`pension sums only:` 0) `, deducted under s 47` 0

-- (3): min(total, 116,400) - insured; nil, not negative (fork F3).
#ASSERT `s 47(a)(3) — the income for a self-employed member of` `S100, self-employed, 100,000` `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 100000
#ASSERT `s 47(a)(3) — the income for a self-employed member of` `M, 60,000 insured salary and 100,000 otherwise` `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 56400
#ASSERT `s 47(a)(3) — the income for a self-employed member of` `E15, an employee on 15,000 a month, paying 6%` `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 0
-- (5): lower of (1) min(total - insured, 116,400) and (2) min(total, 291,000) - max(insured, 116,400).
-- M: (1) 100,000; (2) 160,000 - 116,400 = 43,600.
#ASSERT `s 47(a)(5) — the additional income of` `M, 60,000 insured salary and 100,000 otherwise` `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 43600
-- S100: (1) 100,000; (2) 100,000 - 116,400 is negative: nil.
#ASSERT `s 47(a)(5) — the additional income of` `S100, self-employed, 100,000` `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 0
-- S250: (1) 116,400; (2) 250,000 - 116,400 = 133,600.
#ASSERT `s 47(a)(5) — the additional income of` `S250, self-employed, 250,000` `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 116400
-- The booklet's 24,250 a month for additional income is 2.5 x 9,700, the ceiling of (5)(2).
#ASSERT 2.5 TIMES 9700 EQUALS 24250

§§ `Section 47(a)(4), (7) — insured income, beneficiary member`

#ASSERT `s 47(a)(4) — the insured income is part of the work income:` `E15, an employee on 15,000 a month, paying 6%`
#ASSERT NOT `s 47(a)(4) — the insured income is part of the work income:` (`in` 2026 `, resident` TRUE `, work income` 50000 `, other income` 0 `, insured income` 60000 `, deposits for him` 0 `, sums` (`pension sums only:` 0) `, deducted under s 47` 0)

-- 16% of 165,228 = 26,436.48.
#ASSERT `s 47(a)(7) — the least sum that makes a beneficiary member, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 26436.48
-- The booklet prints 26,436, the shekel below (fork F8).
#ASSERT TRUNC (`s 47(a)(7) — the least sum that makes a beneficiary member, at` `the 2026 amounts`) 0 EQUALS (`the Tax Authority's withholding-booklet figures for sections 45A and 47, for tax year` 2026)'s `the least sum for a beneficiary member, per year`
#ASSERT TRUNC (`s 47(a)(7) — the least sum that makes a beneficiary member, at` `the 2025 amounts`) 0 EQUALS (`the Tax Authority's withholding-booklet figures for sections 45A and 47, for tax year` 2025)'s `the least sum for a beneficiary member, per year`
-- E10: 22,200 is less: not a beneficiary member. E15: 33,300: a beneficiary member.
#ASSERT NOT `s 47(a)(7) — a beneficiary member:` `E10, an employee on 10,000 a month, paying 6%` `, at` `the 2026 amounts`
#ASSERT `s 47(a)(7) — a beneficiary member:` `E15, an employee on 15,000 a month, paying 6%` `, at` `the 2026 amounts`
-- "שלא פחת מ־16%": exactly 26,436.48 is enough; 26,436 is not (the booklet's rounded figure would say it is).
#ASSERT `s 47(a)(7) — a beneficiary member:` (`in` 2026 `, resident` TRUE `, work income` 150000 `, other income` 0 `, insured income` 150000 `, deposits for him` 26436.48 `, sums` (`pension sums only:` 0) `, deducted under s 47` 0) `, at` `the 2026 amounts`
#ASSERT NOT `s 47(a)(7) — a beneficiary member:` (`in` 2026 `, resident` TRUE `, work income` 150000 `, other income` 0 `, insured income` 150000 `, deposits for him` 26436 `, sums` (`pension sums only:` 0) `, deducted under s 47` 0) `, at` `the 2026 amounts`

§§ `Section 45A — an employee's pension contributions`

-- E10 is not a beneficiary member: (d). Qualifying income 116,400, with work income: 7% = 8,148.
-- Limb (2) = min(7,200, 8,148) = 7,200; limb (1) 2,268; the limit 7,200; nothing cut.
-- Credit 35% x 7,200 = 2,520.
#ASSERT (`s 45A(d)-(e) — the limit that governs, for` `E10, an employee on 10,000 a month, paying 6%` `, at` `the 2026 amounts`)'s `the subsection` EQUALS "(d)"
#ASSERT `s 45A(d)(2)(b) — the percentage of qualifying income, for` `E10, an employee on 10,000 a month, paying 6%` `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 8148
#ASSERT `the credit under section 45A for` `E10, an employee on 10,000 a month, paying 6%` `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 2520

-- E15 is a beneficiary member: (e)(2)(b)(2), insured income. Part (a): 7% of min(180,000, 116,400)
-- = 8,148; part (b): 5% of the income not insured, nil. Limb (2) = min(10,800, 8,148) = 8,148.
-- Something is cut, all at 35%, no survivors: 35% x 8,148 = 2,851.8.
#ASSERT (`s 45A(d)-(e) — the limit that governs, for` `E15, an employee on 15,000 a month, paying 6%` `, at` `the 2026 amounts`)'s `the subsection` EQUALS "(e)"
#ASSERT `s 45A(e)(2)(b) — the percentage of income, for` `E15, an employee on 15,000 a month, paying 6%` `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 8148
#ASSERT `the credit under section 45A for` `E15, an employee on 15,000 a month, paying 6%` `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 2851.8
-- Paying 7% (12,600) changes nothing: the limit already binds.
#ASSERT `the credit under section 45A for` `E15, paying 7%` `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 2851.8

-- E5: not a beneficiary member (11,100). Qualifying income 60,000; 7% = 4,200; limb (2) = 3,600.
-- Credit 35% x 3,600 = 1,260.
#ASSERT `the credit under section 45A for` `E5, an employee on 5,000 a month, paying 6%` `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 1260

-- L: qualifying income 20,000; 7% = 1,400; limb (2) = min(1,200, 1,400) = 1,200; limb (1) 2,268
-- governs; the 1,200 paid is within it. Credit 35% x 1,200 = 420.
#ASSERT `the credit under section 45A for` `L, a low earner on 20,000 a year, paying 1,200` `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 420

-- s 47(c): 2,000 of E10's 7,200 deducted under s 47 leaves 5,200; limb (2) 5,200; credit 1,820.
#ASSERT `the credit under section 45A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident` TRUE `, work income` 120000 `, other income` 0 `, insured income` 120000 `, deposits for him` 22200 `, sums` (`pension sums only:` 7200) `, deducted under s 47` 2000) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 1820

-- The same employee in 2025, at the 2025 amounts (average wage 12,536 a month: 16% of the year is
-- 24,069.12; 22,200 is less): (d), and the same 2,520.
#ASSERT `the credit under section 45A for` (`in` 2025 `, resident` TRUE `, work income` 120000 `, other income` 0 `, insured income` 120000 `, deposits for him` 22200 `, sums` (`pension sums only:` 7200) `, deducted under s 47` 0) `, at` `the 2025 amounts` EQUALS 2520

-- A tax year before 2024 is declined.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit under section 45A for` (`in` 2023 `, resident` TRUE `, work income` 120000 `, other income` 0 `, insured income` 120000 `, deposits for him` 22200 `, sums` (`pension sums only:` 7200) `, deducted under s 47` 0) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` BECAUSE "row IL-08 does not hold the text of these sections for a tax year before 2024"

§§ `Section 45A — life insurance, and the two rates`

-- L with 500 of life insurance: total 1,700, within limb (1)'s 2,268, which governs (limb (2) is
-- min(1,700, 1,400) = 1,400). Nothing cut: 25% x 500 + 35% x 1,200 = 125 + 420 = 545.
#ASSERT `the credit under section 45A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident` TRUE `, work income` 20000 `, other income` 0 `, insured income` 20000 `, deposits for him` 3700 `, sums` (`life insurance and pension:` 500 `,` 1200) `, deducted under s 47` 0) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 545
-- The same, not an Israeli resident: (a)(1)'s life insurance is not creditable (fork F4): 420.
#ASSERT `the credit under section 45A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident` FALSE `, work income` 20000 `, other income` 0 `, insured income` 20000 `, deposits for him` 3700 `, sums` (`life insurance and pension:` 500 `,` 1200) `, deducted under s 47` 0) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 420
-- L with 2,000 of life insurance: total 3,200 above the limit 2,268, and the sums are at two rates.
-- Which are credited, the section does not say (fork F1).
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit under section 45A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident` TRUE `, work income` 20000 `, other income` 0 `, insured income` 20000 `, deposits for him` 3700 `, sums` (`life insurance and pension:` 2000 `,` 1200) `, deducted under s 47` 0) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` BECAUSE "section 45A does not say which sums are credited when its limits cut sums of different kinds"

§§ `Section 45A — the provisos`

-- (d)(2)(b)(2), survivors' insurance: E10's salary with pension 4,000 and survivors' insurance
-- 2,000. Limb (2) = min(6,000, 8,148) = 6,000 governs; survivors' 2,000 is above 1.5% of 116,400
-- (1,746). All at 35%: 4,000 + min(2,000, 1,746) = 5,746, within 5% (5,820) and the limit 6,000.
-- Credit 35% x 5,746 = 2,011.1.
#ASSERT `the credit under section 45A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident` TRUE `, work income` 120000 `, other income` 0 `, insured income` 120000 `, deposits for him` 22200 `, sums` (`pension and survivors' insurance:` 4000 `,` 2000) `, deducted under s 47` 0) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 2011.1

-- (d)(2)(b)(2), sums in respect of income not from work: M with pension 10,000 paid by himself
-- (not a beneficiary member). Qualifying income: 60,000 of work income, and of his 100,000 of other
-- income all of it, the room being 164,400 - 60,000 = 104,400: 160,000. 7% = 11,200;
-- limb (2) = min(10,000, 11,200) = 10,000. 5% = 8,000.
-- With 6,000 of the pension in respect of income not from work: within 8,000; credit 3,500.
#ASSERT `the credit under section 45A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident` TRUE `, work income` 60000 `, other income` 100000 `, insured income` 60000 `, deposits for him` 10000 `, sums` (`pension, with a part paid in respect of income not from work:` 10000 `,` 6000) `, deducted under s 47` 0) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 3500
-- With 9,000 of it: the 5% part is capped at 8,000, so 1,000 + 8,000 = 9,000; credit 3,150.
#ASSERT `the credit under section 45A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident` TRUE `, work income` 60000 `, other income` 100000 `, insured income` 60000 `, deposits for him` 10000 `, sums` (`pension, with a part paid in respect of income not from work:` 10000 `,` 9000) `, deducted under s 47` 0) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 3150

-- (d)(2)(b)(1), no work income: 100,000 of other income, 6,000 paid to a pension fund by himself.
-- Qualifying income 100,000; 5% = 5,000; limb (2) 5,000; credit 35% x 5,000 = 1,750.
#ASSERT `the credit under section 45A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident` TRUE `, work income` 0 `, other income` 100000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 6000 `, sums` (`pension sums only:` 6000) `, deducted under s 47` 0) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 1750

-- (e)(2)(b)(2), survivors' insurance within part (a)'s 1.5% (1,746): E15 with 1,000 of it.
-- All at 35%: min(8,148, 11,800) = 8,148; credit 2,851.8.
#ASSERT `the credit under section 45A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident` TRUE `, work income` 180000 `, other income` 0 `, insured income` 180000 `, deposits for him` 33300 `, sums` (`pension and survivors' insurance:` 10800 `,` 1000) `, deducted under s 47` 0) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 2851.8
-- With 2,000 of it: more than part (a)'s 1,746, and whether the rest belongs to part (b) the
-- subsection does not say (fork F1).
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit under section 45A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident` TRUE `, work income` 180000 `, other income` 0 `, insured income` 180000 `, deposits for him` 33300 `, sums` (`pension and survivors' insurance:` 10800 `,` 2000) `, deducted under s 47` 0) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` BECAUSE "section 45A(e)(2)(b)(2) does not say to which of its two parts a survivors' insurance sum belongs"

§§ `Section 45A — the floor of limb (1) after the provisos (version 0.2.0, D187)`

-- P, an employee not a beneficiary member (12,500 deposited for him): 100,000 of work income, all
-- insured. Qualifying income 100,000; (d)(2)(b)(2): 7% = 7,000; the survivors' proviso 1.5% = 1,500;
-- the 5% proviso 5,000. Fork F5(i): the total credited is the higher of 2,268 and limb (2) as its
-- provisos limit it, within the sums paid.
GIVEN `pension`   IS A NUMBER
      `survivors` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47`
`P, paying pension` `pension` `and survivors' insurance` `survivors` MEANS
    `in` 2026 `, resident` TRUE `, work income` 100000 `, other income` 0 `, insured income` 100000 `, deposits for him` 12500 `, sums` (`pension and survivors' insurance:` `pension` `,` `survivors`) `, deducted under s 47` 0

-- D187: 5,000 of survivors' insurance only. Limb (2) = min(5,000, 7,000) = 5,000 before the proviso,
-- min(5,000, 1,500) = 1,500 after it; the higher of 2,268 and 1,500 is 2,268; credited
-- min(5,000, 2,268) = 2,268; credit 35% x 2,268 = 793.8 (version 0.1.0: 525).
#ASSERT `the credit under section 45A for` (`P, paying pension` 0 `and survivors' insurance` 5000) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 793.8
-- The cliff of version 0.1.0 is gone: 2,268 and 2,269 both give 793.8 (version 0.1.0: 793.8, 525).
#ASSERT `the credit under section 45A for` (`P, paying pension` 0 `and survivors' insurance` 2268) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 793.8
#ASSERT `the credit under section 45A for` (`P, paying pension` 0 `and survivors' insurance` 2269) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 793.8
-- 500 of pension and 3,000 of survivors' insurance: limb (2) = min(3,500, 7,000) = 3,500 before the
-- proviso, 500 + 1,500 = 2,000 after it; the higher of 2,268 and 2,000 is 2,268; credit 793.8
-- (version 0.1.0: 35% x 2,000 = 700).
#ASSERT `the credit under section 45A for` (`P, paying pension` 500 `and survivors' insurance` 3000) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 793.8
-- 1,000 and 3,000: after the proviso 2,500, above the floor: credit 35% x 2,500 = 875 (as before).
#ASSERT `the credit under section 45A for` (`P, paying pension` 1000 `and survivors' insurance` 3000) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 875

-- (d)(2)(b)(1), no work income: 100,000 of other income, 5,000 of survivors' insurance only.
-- Qualifying income 100,000; 5% = 5,000; limb (2) 5,000 before the proviso, 1,500 after it; the
-- floor governs: 793.8 (version 0.1.0: 525).
#ASSERT `the credit under section 45A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident` TRUE `, work income` 0 `, other income` 100000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 0 `, sums` (`pension and survivors' insurance:` 0 `,` 5000) `, deducted under s 47` 0) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 793.8

-- (e)(2)(b)(2): a beneficiary member (30,000 deposited for him), 60,000 of insured work income and
-- 80,000 of other income, 4,000 of survivors' insurance only. Insured qualifying income 60,000;
-- part (b)'s income min(140,000 - 60,000, 232,800 - 60,000) = 80,000; limb (2) = min(4,000,
-- 4,200 + 4,000) = 4,000 before the provisos. Part (a)'s survivors' cap is 900, so the provisos'
-- effect turns on the part the survivors' sums belong to (fork F1); but under any attribution they
-- are credited at most 900 + 1.5% x 80,000 = 2,100, below 2,268: limb (1) governs whichever part,
-- credited min(4,000, 2,268) = 2,268, credit 793.8 (version 0.1.0: declined).
#ASSERT `the credit under section 45A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident` TRUE `, work income` 60000 `, other income` 80000 `, insured income` 60000 `, deposits for him` 30000 `, sums` (`pension and survivors' insurance:` 0 `,` 4000) `, deducted under s 47` 0) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 793.8
-- With 100,000 of other income the most under any attribution is 900 + 1,500 = 2,400, above
-- 2,268: the answer turns on the part, and is declined (fork F1).
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit under section 45A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident` TRUE `, work income` 60000 `, other income` 100000 `, insured income` 60000 `, deposits for him` 30000 `, sums` (`pension and survivors' insurance:` 0 `,` 4000) `, deducted under s 47` 0) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` BECAUSE "section 45A(e)(2)(b)(2) does not say to which of its two parts a survivors' insurance sum belongs"

§§ `Section 45A — life insurance alone (version 0.2.0, D183)`

-- P with 6,000 of life insurance only: limb (2) = min(6,000, 7,000) = 6,000; the 5% proviso cuts the
-- life insurance to 5,000; the higher of 2,268 and 5,000 is 5,000; credit 25% x 5,000 = 1,250
-- (version 0.1.0: declined, "sums of different kinds").
#ASSERT `the credit under section 45A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident` TRUE `, work income` 100000 `, other income` 0 `, insured income` 100000 `, deposits for him` 12500 `, sums` (`life insurance and pension:` 6000 `,` 0) `, deducted under s 47` 0) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 1250
-- 5,000: nothing is cut, 1,250. 5,001: cut to 5,000, 1,250 (version 0.1.0: declined).
#ASSERT `the credit under section 45A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident` TRUE `, work income` 100000 `, other income` 0 `, insured income` 100000 `, deposits for him` 12500 `, sums` (`life insurance and pension:` 5000 `,` 0) `, deducted under s 47` 0) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 1250
#ASSERT `the credit under section 45A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident` TRUE `, work income` 100000 `, other income` 0 `, insured income` 100000 `, deposits for him` 12500 `, sums` (`life insurance and pension:` 5001 `,` 0) `, deducted under s 47` 0) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 1250
-- (d)(2)(b)(1), no work income: 100,000 of other income and 6,000 of life insurance only. 5% of the
-- qualifying income is 5,000; no proviso of (b)(1) reaches life insurance; the total limit 5,000 cuts
-- it: credit 25% x 5,000 = 1,250 (version 0.1.0: declined).
#ASSERT `the credit under section 45A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident` TRUE `, work income` 0 `, other income` 100000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 0 `, sums` (`life insurance and pension:` 6000 `,` 0) `, deducted under s 47` 0) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 1250
-- A beneficiary member (30,000 deposited for him) on 20,000 of insured work income, with 2,500 of
-- life insurance: (e)(2)(b)(2), 7% x 20,000 = 1,400; limb (1)'s 2,268 governs; credited
-- min(2,500, 2,268) = 2,268, credit 25% x 2,268 = 567 (version 0.1.0: declined).
#ASSERT `the credit under section 45A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident` TRUE `, work income` 20000 `, other income` 0 `, insured income` 20000 `, deposits for him` 30000 `, sums` (`life insurance and pension:` 2500 `,` 0) `, deducted under s 47` 0) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 567
-- E15 (a beneficiary member) with 7,000 of life insurance only: part (a)'s 5% of 116,400 is 5,820,
-- and part (b) has no cap on life insurance; whether the rest belongs to part (b) the subsection does
-- not say, and the most under any attribution (5,820 + 5% x 0) is above 2,268: declined (fork F1).
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit under section 45A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident` TRUE `, work income` 180000 `, other income` 0 `, insured income` 180000 `, deposits for him` 33300 `, sums` (`life insurance and pension:` 7000 `,` 0) `, deducted under s 47` 0) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` BECAUSE "section 45A(e)(2)(b)(2) does not say to which of its two parts a life-insurance sum belongs"

§§ `Section 45A(b1) and (e) — a beneficiary member's child, and both parts of (e)(2)(b)(2)`

-- E15 with 2,000 paid to a provident fund for a child of 18 or more: (b1) applies, all at 35%;
-- 12,800 against the limit 8,148: 2,851.8.
#ASSERT `the credit under section 45A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident` TRUE `, work income` 180000 `, other income` 0 `, insured income` 180000 `, deposits for him` 33300 `, sums` (`pension and a child's provident fund:` 10800 `,` 2000) `, deducted under s 47` 0) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 2851.8
-- E10 is not a beneficiary member: (b1) gives him nothing for the child, and his credit stays 2,520.
#ASSERT `s 45A(b1) — the child's pension sums that may be credited, for` (`in` 2026 `, resident` TRUE `, work income` 120000 `, other income` 0 `, insured income` 120000 `, deposits for him` 22200 `, sums` (`pension and a child's provident fund:` 7200 `,` 2000) `, deducted under s 47` 0) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit under section 45A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident` TRUE `, work income` 120000 `, other income` 0 `, insured income` 120000 `, deposits for him` 22200 `, sums` (`pension and a child's provident fund:` 7200 `,` 2000) `, deducted under s 47` 0) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 2520

-- (e)(2)(b)(1), a beneficiary member with no insured income: 200,000 of business income, 30,000
-- paid to a pension fund by himself. 5% of min(200,000, 232,800) = 10,000; credit 3,500.
#ASSERT `the credit under section 45A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident` TRUE `, work income` 0 `, other income` 200000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 30000 `, sums` (`pension sums only:` 30000) `, deducted under s 47` 0) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 3500

-- (e)(2)(b)(2), both parts: M with 30,000 deposited for him (a beneficiary member) and 15,000 paid
-- by himself. Part (a): 7% x min(60,000, 60,000) = 4,200. Part (b): 5% x min(100,000,
-- 232,800 - min(116,400, 60,000) = 172,800) = 5,000. Limit 9,200; credit 35% x 9,200 = 3,220.
#ASSERT `s 45A(e)(2)(b) — the percentage of income, for` (`in` 2026 `, resident` TRUE `, work income` 60000 `, other income` 100000 `, insured income` 60000 `, deposits for him` 30000 `, sums` (`pension sums only:` 15000) `, deducted under s 47` 0) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 9200
#ASSERT `the credit under section 45A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident` TRUE `, work income` 60000 `, other income` 100000 `, insured income` 60000 `, deposits for him` 30000 `, sums` (`pension sums only:` 15000) `, deducted under s 47` 0) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 3220

§§ `Section 45A(f) — a self-employed member's deposits`

GIVEN `deposited` IS A NUMBER
      `deducted under section 32(14)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47`
`a self-employed member on 100,000 who deposited` `deposited` `, with a deduction under section 32(14)(b):` `deducted under section 32(14)(b)` MEANS
    `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47` WITH
        `tax year`                                                                      IS 2026
        `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                                           IS TRUE
        `taxable income from work, before the deductions under sections 47 and 47A`     IS 0
        `taxable income not from work, before the deductions under sections 47 and 47A` IS 100000
        `taxable income from a business or profession`                                  IS 100000
        `insured income`                                                                IS 0
        `sums paid in the tax year to a pension provident fund in respect of the individual's income` IS `deposited`
        `sums paid, for section 45A`                                                    IS `pension sums only:` 0
        `sums paid, for section 47`                                                     IS `no sums for section 47`
        `sums deducted under section 47(b) or (b1)`                                     IS 0
        `sums deposited to a pension provident fund as a self-employed member for himself, not credited under section 45A(b)` IS `deposited`
        `a deduction was made for him under section 32(14)(b) for preferred insurance against loss of working capacity`      IS `deducted under section 32(14)(b)`
        `within a class for which regulations under section 47(d) set higher deductions`                                    IS FALSE
        `a foreign worker`                                                                                                  IS FALSE

-- 0.5% of min(100,000, 2 x 116,400 - 0) = 500 may be credited; of 1,000 deposited, 35% x 500 = 175.
#ASSERT `s 45A(f) — the credit for a self-employed member's deposits, for` (`a self-employed member on 100,000 who deposited` 1000 `, with a deduction under section 32(14)(b):` FALSE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 175
-- Of 300 deposited, all of it: 105.
#ASSERT `s 45A(f) — the credit for a self-employed member's deposits, for` (`a self-employed member on 100,000 who deposited` 300 `, with a deduction under section 32(14)(b):` FALSE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 105
-- With a deduction under s 32(14)(b): nothing under (f).
#ASSERT `s 45A(f) — the credit for a self-employed member's deposits, for` (`a self-employed member on 100,000 who deposited` 1000 `, with a deduction under section 32(14)(b):` TRUE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 0
-- The section as a whole for him: nothing under (a)-(e) (no sums), 175 under (f).
#ASSERT `the credit under section 45A for` (`a self-employed member on 100,000 who deposited` 1000 `, with a deduction under section 32(14)(b):` FALSE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 175

§§ `Section 48A — a foreign worker`

GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47`
GIVETH AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47`
`as a foreign worker:` i MEANS
    `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47` WITH
        `tax year`                                                                      IS i's `tax year`
        `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                                           IS i's `an Israeli resident in the tax year`
        `taxable income from work, before the deductions under sections 47 and 47A`     IS i's `taxable income from work, before the deductions under sections 47 and 47A`
        `taxable income not from work, before the deductions under sections 47 and 47A` IS i's `taxable income not from work, before the deductions under sections 47 and 47A`
        `taxable income from a business or profession`                                  IS i's `taxable income from a business or profession`
        `insured income`                                                                IS i's `insured income`
        `sums paid in the tax year to a pension provident fund in respect of the individual's income` IS i's `sums paid in the tax year to a pension provident fund in respect of the individual's income`
        `sums paid, for section 45A`                                                    IS i's `sums paid, for section 45A`
        `sums paid, for section 47`                                                     IS i's `sums paid, for section 47`
        `sums deducted under section 47(b) or (b1)`                                     IS i's `sums deducted under section 47(b) or (b1)`
        `sums deposited to a pension provident fund as a self-employed member for himself, not credited under section 45A(b)` IS i's `sums deposited to a pension provident fund as a self-employed member for himself, not credited under section 45A(b)`
        `a deduction was made for him under section 32(14)(b) for preferred insurance against loss of working capacity`      IS i's `a deduction was made for him under section 32(14)(b) for preferred insurance against loss of working capacity`
        `within a class for which regulations under section 47(d) set higher deductions`                                    IS i's `within a class for which regulations under section 47(d) set higher deductions`
        `a foreign worker`                                                                                                  IS TRUE

-- E10 as a foreign worker: the section would credit 2,520, which the 2014 Regulations may take away.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit under section 45A for` (`as a foreign worker:` `E10, an employee on 10,000 a month, paying 6%`) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` BECAUSE "section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model"
-- A foreign worker who paid nothing: the section gives nothing, and nothing can be taken away.
#ASSERT `the credit under section 45A for` (`as a foreign worker:` (`a 2026 earner of` 120000 `from work and` 0 `otherwise`)) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 0
